{
 "id": "158-9",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "Now, to get you started, I want you to focus on your tasks and communicate with the team only when asked.",
  "This will help you settle in and ensure you're not overwhelmed.",
  "Always use docstrings in your functions.",
  "Clear and concise documentation is crucial in our team.",
  "Most monitors have built-in settings for height, tilt, and distance.",
  "Play around with those adjustments until you find a comfortable viewing position.",
  "Remember, your eyes should be level with the top of the screen.",
  "Your keyboard and mouse should be positioned so that your arms are relaxed and your wrists don't bend unnaturally.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out if you need further assistance or if you have any questions.",
  "By actively listening and responding to their concerns, we can build a more inclusive and supportive workplace.",
  "I want to give you a few instructions to follow when writing your functions from now on.",
  "Going forward, I want you to add the '@count_calls' decorator from the 'pedantic' module to all your functions.",
  "This will help us keep track of how often each function is used, which is valuable information for code maintenance and optimization.",
  "Additionally, when naming your functions, always include a single digit.",
  "This will help us quickly identify and differentiate between functions, especially when we're working with larger codebases or collaborating on projects.",
  "Remember, these practices will not only benefit your own code but also contribute to the overall quality and maintainability of the projects you work on here at PACE.",
  "And it's important to create an environment where employees feel comfortable speaking up, asking questions, and sharing their ideas."
 ],
